  <h1>oeneyeOS - Floppy Max 2.88MB + VHD</h1>

  <p>A: oeneyeOS.img (2.88M) | B: data.img (2.88M) | C: date.img</p>
  <p>
    D: <a href="https://github.com/Colegio-San-Caio/demo-repository/releases/download/v1.0/GNUoeneyeALPINEunix.img">GNUoeneyeALPINEunix.img</a> (357 MB) | 
    SHA-256: <code>a91847bcda43baca5a643be9769ebfd17bd5c371718ed8eb63d9e5f628c49188</code>
  </p>
  <p>
    X: <a href="https://github.com/Colegio-San-Caio/demo-repository/releases/download/v1.0/workshop.img">workshop.img</a> (1.4 MB) | 
    <a href="https://github.com/Colegio-San-Caio/demo-repository/releases/download/v1.0/fily.img">fily.img</a> (360 KB)
  </p>
  <p>
    workshop.img SHA-256: <code>8653aa17d505212d429548e197e3e6a86a5295552a1b75aac896ab5b00b67fda</code><br>
    fily.img SHA-256: <code>00accd519026d7b17f738bdf1eb96151c853b8a97fdcbb807d093c789786a14a</code>
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="oeneyeOS.img">Download A</a> | 
    <a href="data.img">Download B</a> | 
    <a href="date.img">Download C</a>
  </p>
  <code>qemu-system-i386 -fda oeneyeOS.img -fdb data.img -hda date.img</code>
  <p>Back up important data before using the disk-image tools. A defect in disk-writing code can damage data.</p>

  <h2>License (EULA)</h2>
  <p>Free to use, modify and share. Don't present a modified version as the official release. The original oeneye code is MIT-licensed, the software is provided as is, and it is not security-certified.</p>
  <p>
    <a href="assets/OENEYE_EULA.pdf">oeneye OS EULA, version 1.0 (PDF)</a><br>
    <span>DOI: <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22978006">10.5281/zenodo.22978006</a></span>
  </p>

