  <h2>Verify your download</h2>
  <p>SHA-256 checksums for the disk images. Put both images and the checksum file in one folder, then run the check.</p>
  <code>2741dfdbc24c3514ffcd04411a108e3b9b76ad0a7522c2a4b360cdbb27b9d42d  oeneyeOS.img
1b7b350b66f56a4646573de32f7fea22a050cdf99672d8751c49043abc82ebab  data.img</code><br>
  <code>sha256sum --check checksum.sha256</code>
  <p><a href="assets/checksum.sha256">checksum.sha256</a></p>
  <p>A matching checksum shows the file is the one published here. It doesn't prove the contents are safe.</p>

  <h2>Demo: python3 emu_dos.py</h2>
  <p>Runs in your browser with Pyodide (Python compiled to WebAssembly). Nothing is sent to a server.</p>
  <div>
    <div><span>emu_dos.py</span><span><a href="emu_dos.py" target="_blank">Raw</a></span></div>
    <pre>Loading emu_dos.py...</pre>
  </div>

  <pre>$ python3 emu_dos.py
(press Run)</pre>

